      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name}: I actually do use multiple object pools for identical items, but I've found an interesting use case in using an object pool to drive a random room generator.  Having access to the pointer would enable calling specific rooms to place them if desired, as well as reset the pointer back to start of the pool on a fresh layout generation without having to Shuffle.\n\nIt would also just be a very neat and tidy way to network-sync a whole lot of general objects without needing to condition them with their own bools/animations/etc.  Just let the pool handle whether it need be on or not and call what you want once.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
